; The root delegates example. and carries no DS for it, so everything
; below is insecure.  That is on purpose: this scenario is about what a
; resolver does with a wrong rcode, and a signed zone would give it a
; second, different reason to distrust the answer.
$ORIGIN .
$TTL 3600
@		IN	SOA	ns.root. root.root. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@		IN	NS	ns.root.
ns.root.	IN	A	{{ROOT_ADDR}}
example.	IN	NS	ns.example.
ns.example.	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
